Implement real file transfer.

Example:

```bash
termlink send ./project.zip
```

Send to the entire group:

```bash
termlink send ./project.zip --group
```

Send to a specific peer:

```bash
termlink send ./project.zip --to Rahul
```

Transfer prompt:

```text
Incoming file

Filename: project.zip
Size: 450 MB
Sender: AADI-PC

Accept transfer? [Y/n]
```

Implement:

- Single file transfer
- Multiple file transfer
- Group file transfer
- Peer-specific transfer
- File size display
- Transfer progress
- Transfer speed
- Estimated remaining time
- Pause
- Resume where feasible
- Cancel
- Destination selection
- Filename conflict handling
- Recipient acceptance
- Rejection
- Chunked transfers
- File integrity verification
- SHA-256 verification
- Error handling
- Interrupted transfer recovery
- Transfer history stored locally

Never silently overwrite existing files.

Never execute received files automatically.

## Transfer protocol

Design a robust transfer protocol.

Use chunked data transmission.

Include:

- Transfer ID
- Metadata
- File name
- File size
- Chunk indexes
- Chunk checksums
- File checksum
- Transfer status
- Acknowledgements
- Resume state

Avoid loading entire large files into memory.

Use streaming APIs.

Implement backpressure.

